{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgTLfXCfDs7Vc4uD8E3x8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`test_large_sequence` fails because the test and the code disagree about what a 5-digit sequence should look like. I ran it with `unittest` to confirm.\n\n- **The code:** `invoice_number` in `invoice.py` formats the sequence as `{seq:04}`. That pads to at least 4 digits and never cuts digits off, so 12345 comes out as `INV-2026-12345`.\n- **The test:** it expects `INV-2026-2345` for `invoice_number(2026, 12345)`. That would mean keeping only the last 4 digits (`seq % 10000`).\n\nThe code isn't broken. The expected value looks wrong, or at least it assumes behavior the code was never given. Dropping the leading digit would make two different invoices, 2345 and 12345, get the same number, which is a bad outcome for invoice IDs.\n\nI haven't changed anything. Which behavior do you want?\n1. **Keep the current code and fix the test** so it expects `INV-2026-12345`. This is my default, and it avoids duplicate numbers.\n2. **Cap the sequence at 4 digits.** Truncating would give the test's value, but I'd prefer to raise an error on `seq > 9999` instead. Silent truncation produces duplicate numbers."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":455,"cache_read_input_tokens":39368,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":455},"output_tokens":412,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ced05d5a-a27f-4cf4-9627-0c21c297ea44","uuid":"66d8b94e-a381-49f0-96e1-177d8ff4e7d3","timestamp":"2026-10-27T20:03:23.658Z","request_id":"req_011CgTLfWuYq911W2ngNumTE"}
